; xhcicmf.inf - xhcicm.sys as the upper filter of the Thunderbolt and USB4
; tunnel ports, the 32-bit package's NT-only filter INF (design record 21
; sections 3.2, 3.3 and 6.2, decision D2; design record 22 section 3.7;
; roadmap-usb4.md tasks 39-A.1 and 40-0.2).
;
; NT targets only. Windows 98 SE's and ME's engines DO read a "$Windows NT$"
; INF (runs/run-39.md, 39-0.4): a plain VEN&DEV line was installed on a
; bridge there, and a WDM driver on a bridge devnode breaks the bridge on
; Windows 98 (record 21 section 6.1). So this file has no undecorated
; install section, every model line is in the &CC_0604 form (which 98 SE's
; and ME's automatic search did not choose), and the package stages it in
; an nt\ subdirectory of each flavour directory, never beside xhcicm.inf
; where a 98 user points the wizard (CM-NO9XBRIDGE). Its one source disk
; is that directory itself, which holds its own copy of xhcicm.sys (the
; same bytes as the flavour directory's): Vista's and 7's driver store
; refuses a source outside the INF's directory (SetupCopyOEMInf error
; 0xA1, ERROR_BAD_PATHNAME, read 2026-10-15 on 7 SP1 x86).
;
; Decision D2, read by task 39-0.4: the device-specific route. The install
; sections keep pci.sys as the port's service by including and needing
; machine.inf's PCI_DRV, PCI_DRV.HW and PCI_DRV.Services and add xhcicm as
; a device-specific UpperFilters value; Windows 2000 takes the INF
; unforced, XP and 7 only forced (the unsigned INF ranks 0x8005 against
; machine.inf's 0x2004): the installer forces it, a user by hand uses Have
; Disk. Each port of a switch carries its switch's id; the filter attaches
; to each and acts only on the ports the NHI verifies and assigns. Every
; line must carry &CC_0604: the driver takes the filter role by that class
; (src\cm\cm_vals.c).
;
; This INF becomes the port's device INF, so its description replaces the
; OS's bridge name: TbBridgeDesc for the Thunderbolt 2 and 3 generation's
; ports (Falcon, Alpine and Titan Ridge, Ice Lake), U4BridgeDesc for the
; USB4 generation's (Maple Ridge, Tiger Lake onward, Barlow Ridge, AMD,
; ASMedia), BridgeDesc for the emulator's generic bridges (record 21
; section 3.3; the gate's CM-DESC).
;
; The filter reads no registry value; the NHI's values are xhcicm.inf's.
;
; scripts\inf-gate\check-cm-inf.ps1 -Filter gates this file on every build.
;
; ASCII only, CRLF line endings.

[Version]
Signature="$Windows NT$"
Class=System
ClassGUID={4D36E97D-E325-11CE-BFC1-08002BE10318}
Provider=%Provider%
; Must equal src\xhci_version.h.
DriverVer=10/17/2026,3.0.0.0

[Manufacturer]
%Mfg%=CmFilterModels,NTx86.6.0

[CmFilterModels]
; Record 21 section 3.3's list. The discrete controllers' switch ports;
; 15C0 has been read by this project, every other line is untested.
